// ============================================================================
// LearnedFields.def - the V3 learned-tail-field manifest (data-only file).
// ============================================================================
// One X_LEARNED(field_name) line per tail field the SDK has LEARNED to
// read. The field itself is declared at the tail of OdinOdomData in
// odin_lidar_def.h; this manifest only REGISTERS it - both width and tail
// offset are derived from the public struct's own layout at expansion time,
// so the manifest order is irrelevant and the declaration stays the single
// source of truth.
//
// Learning a new field = exactly TWO touches:
//   1. declare it at the tail of OdinOdomData in odin_lidar_def.h (with a
//      default value) and bump the struct's sizeof assert;
//   2. add ONE line here:   X_LEARNED(field_name)
// V3/OdomEntry.hpp expands this manifest into the conversion (the learned
// lines) and into the kLearnedTail ledger (the width sum), so:
//   - a field declared but not listed here fails the ledger assert
//     (compile error naming the fix - never a silently always-default field);
//   - a line without its declaration fails to compile (offsetof finds no
//     member).
//
// Contract: firmware appends these fields AFTER `type`, in frozen
// append-only order, WITHOUT a version bump (up to kOdomMaxTailExt bytes
// per entry). Reshuffling the tail shifts downstream offsets into wrong
// fields and requires a version bump instead.
//
// The macro is named X_LEARNED (not X) on purpose: this file gets included
// WHILE OdomGenerations.def is being expanded (its layout includes pull in
// V3/OdomEntry.hpp), and nested X-macro expansions must not share a macro
// name - an inner #undef would kill the outer definition mid-expansion.
//
// Included multiple times by consumers that #define X_LEARNED first and
// #undef it afterwards. The #error below refuses an include without a
// definition. No include guard on purpose - the whole point is re-expansion.
#ifndef X_LEARNED
#error "Define X_LEARNED(FIELD) before including LearnedFields.def"
#endif

// NOTHING LEARNED YET. The first entry looks like:
// X_LEARNED(test)
